          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mtilsfq4au5hoika",
          "message": {
            "text": "The no-open check lives at the shared OS side-effect boundary because per-command flags proved insufficient: an automated caller that forgot --no-open opened both svg-scrubber and SVG Demo Test Review in the user's real Chrome. Vitest's inherited sentinel protects child CLIs, while DOMOTIONNOOPEN=1 covers non-Vitest automation such as merged coverage. Normal interactive CLI behavior is unchanged.",
            "markdown": "The no-open check lives at the shared OS side-effect boundary because per-command flags proved insufficient: an automated caller that forgot `--no-open` opened both svg-scrubber and SVG Demo Test Review in the user's real Chrome. Vitest's inherited sentinel protects child CLIs, while `DOMOTION_NO_OPEN=1` covers non-Vitest automation such as merged coverage. Normal interactive CLI behavior is unchanged."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/cli/common.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 74,
                  "endLine": 84,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "export function shouldOpenInBrowser(env: NodeJS.ProcessEnv = process.env): boolean {\n  return env.VITEST == null && env.DOMOTION_NO_OPEN !== \"1\";\n}\n\nexport async function openInBrowser(url: string): Promise<void> {\n  // Test code must never steal focus by launching the user's real browser.\n  // Keep this guard here, at the final shared side-effect boundary, so a new\n  // caller cannot bypass it by forgetting its own `--no-open` flag. Vitest\n  // exports VITEST to its workers and their inherited child processes;\n  // DOMOTION_NO_OPEN covers other automated runners.\n  if (!shouldOpenInBrowser()) return;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
